# hsim_runtime_lib: link the portable runtime with -lhsim_runtime

Goal: replace today's compile command (4 runtime sources + linker script +
--start-group incantation) with:

```sh
riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc -march=rv64gc -mabi=lp64d -O2 \
  -B $HSIM/build/runtime -specs=hsim.specs hello.c -o hello.elf
```

`-B` tells gcc/ld where the artifacts live (startfiles, -L, specs lookup);
`-specs=hsim.specs` applies them. Raw `-lhsim_runtime` also works for
non-gcc-driver build systems (documented form, see F2).

## Artifacts (built into build/runtime/)

| file | contents |
|---|---|
| libhsim_runtime.a | trap.o, handler.o, vplat_syscalls.o |
| crt0.o | boot code; OUTSIDE the archive: nothing references `_start`, so the linker would never extract it from a .a (same reason toolchains ship crt0.o next to libc.a) |
| hsim.ld | linker script (today's tests/fixtures/test.ld, base 0x00100000) |
| hsim.specs | startfile -> crt0.o, -Thsim.ld, lib sequence -> `--start-group -lhsim_runtime -lc -lgcc --end-group`, no -lgloss |

Archive pull-chain: crt0.o calls init_mtvec/_exit -> handler.o +
vplat_syscalls.o; handler.o references m_trap_entry -> trap.o.

## Decisions

- Library = vplat flavor ONLY (engine-portable). The semihosting flavor
  (-lgloss_vh) stays a fixture-internal recipe; shipping it would re-open
  the "works on fast, traps on cycle" cliff.
- Sources move tests/fixtures/runtime/ -> runtime/ (user-facing code does
  not live under tests/). rt_c_helpers.h stays test-side: csr markers are
  not portable (MILMB, see one_elf_three_engines.md).
- vplat fixtures relink against the built archive, so the e2e suite
  regression-tests the shipped artifact.

