## Notes

- The --start-group in the specs lib sequence is required: newlib's `write`
  resolves to our `_write` only if the linker can revisit
  libhsim_runtime.a after searching -lc.
- hsim.specs contains no absolute paths (portability): crt0.o is found via
  startfile prefixes (-B), hsim.ld via the -L that gcc derives from -B,
  libhsim_runtime.a via the same -L.
- -march/-mabi stay on the user command line: they are per-program choices
  (rv64gc vs rv64gcv), not runtime properties.
